From: Kurcide <contact@aevonix.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Optional online FP8 for the audio-decoder (MTP) projections

The MTP projections are plain nn.Linear, so they have no quant_method and the
loader's process_weights_after_loading never reaches them. This quantizes
them after the decoder's own weight loader has run, which is required: that
loader copies in place into pre-existing bf16 parameters and shards gate/up
into the two halves of gate_up_proj.

Off unless DRAMA3_MTP_FP8=1. Scope is selectable so the most audio-sensitive
weights can stay bf16:
  DRAMA3_MTP_FP8_PROJ       which projections (default: all five)
  DRAMA3_MTP_FP8_GROUPS     shared_layers and/or residual_layers
  DRAMA3_MTP_FP8_SKIP_LAST  keep the last N residual layers bf16
  DRAMA3_MTP_FP8_HEADS      include the codebook heads (default 1)

Per-output-channel scales, dynamic per-token activations. Every target is
validated before any module is replaced, so a rejected config fails the load
instead of leaving a half-converted tower.

NOTE: this disables the fused MTP tower by construction, because that path
requires exactly nn.Linear with bf16 weights. The two are mutually exclusive.
---
--- a/sglang_omni/models/fishaudio_drama3/sglang_model.py
+++ b/sglang_omni/models/fishaudio_drama3/sglang_model.py
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 from __future__ import annotations
 
 import dataclasses
+import os
 from collections.abc import Iterable, Iterator
 
 import torch
@@ -361,3 +362,13 @@
             pass
         self.lm_head.weight_loader(self.lm_head.weight, lm_head_weights[0])
         load_audio_decoder_weights(self.audio_decoder, decoder_weights)
+        if os.environ.get("DRAMA3_MTP_FP8", "0") == "1":
+            # The manual loader needs the original bf16 parameters above.
+            from sglang_omni.models.fishaudio_drama3.mtp_fp8 import (
+                quantize_mtp_after_loading,
+            )
+
+            quantize_mtp_after_loading(
+                self.audio_decoder,
+                include_heads=os.environ.get("DRAMA3_MTP_FP8_HEADS", "1") == "1",
+            )
